"B-008\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-009\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states the header is called Retry-After.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Its value is a whole number of seconds to wait.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states the header value is a whole number of seconds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text discusses the header in rate-limit contexts but does not explicitly state it appears on every refusal the gateway sends.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The body of the refusal is JSON\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-013\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"evidence\": \"It names what the gateway calls the \\\"window\\\" it counted in. It names the cap and the tier as well.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text confirms the body contains the cap, window, and tier, but does not explicitly describe them as 'plain fields'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-014\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The body is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states the body is for the human reading the log afterwards.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-015\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Four rules, given in the order they should be applied.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states there are four rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-016\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it does the same on the 503 path\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states the same rule holds on the 503 path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-017\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not explicitly compare the sizes of safe-to-retry responses versus non-success responses.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-018\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A 200 wants nothing\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this; 'needs' and 'wants' are synonymous.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-019\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 429 wants the stated wait\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this; 'needs' and 'wants' are synonymous.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-020\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this; 'can be' and 'may be' are synonymous.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-021\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and a 503 is the overload path\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states 503 is the overload path, which indicates platform overload.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-022\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-023\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"1000 is 10 times 100, not 50 times; the text contradicts this claim by stating the default is 100.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-024\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"it is measured over exactly the same window\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states batch uses the same window as default, not a separate counting scheme.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-025\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"it is measured over exactly the same window\\\" and \\\"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text entails that window, header, and body are identical for both tiers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-026\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-027\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \